<title>GERMANY: Daimler plans more shifts at German plant.</title>
<headline>Daimler plans more shifts at German plant.</headline>
<dateline>SINDELFINGEN, Germany 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG plans to introduce special Saturday shifts at its Sindelfingen car assembly plant, the works council at the plant said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The council said that as well as special shifts already arranged for May, June and July, the company wanted to run an additional shift on most Saturdays until the end of the year.</p>
<p>That would boost car production by 14,000, the works council said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
